      "organism_not_in_bundle": "fruit fly",
      "of_clause": "I want a fruit fly that lives longer",
      "reason": "organism \"fruit fly\" has no reference parameter set in this engine (it holds measured parameters for: zebrafish, flying fish, winged zebrafish, wingless flying fish, TFF, the ff-zf chimera). It is not mapped to a \"close\" one, because the nearest fish is not this animal. A taxon-based design can still be built from it: see spec.taxon, organism_create {taxon} and organism_from_blueprint. The rest of this clause IS parsed: any criterion in it is on the spec, and will be judged once a parameter set for this clade exists."
     },
     {
      "text": "I want a fruit fly that lives longer",
      "reason": "no criterion, organism or edit recognised"
     }
    ],
    "validation_ok": false,
    "a_bug_this_run_found": "Before this run the same sentence produced a GLIDE criterion. familyGlide matches the free-standing word \"fly\", `fruit fly` contains one, and the parser read the name of the animal as a requirement that it be able to fly -- a criterion nobody asked for, attached to a request about lifespan. Two-word insect names ending in \"fly\" are now organism names and are taken out of the clause before the criterion families read it."
   }
